Use this command only from the clean managed `master` worktree.

Run the helper directly from the current project directory:

If the agent shell tool supports `timeout_ms`, run this lifecycle command with `timeout_ms >= 3900000` by default so the outer shell outlives all bounded 1C Designer/Enterprise operations. Do not use `120000 ms` or another short default.

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\.agents\skills\1c-workflow\scripts\run-itl-command.ps1 -- -Action refresh-all-dev-branches
```

The helper synchronizes `master` exactly once, pins the resulting commit, then refreshes every active ready `itldev/*` branch with at most two workers. A failed branch does not cancel the others. On success with a non-empty `userReport`, return exactly that Russian Markdown report. On failure, return the bounded aggregate report and read only the last 80 lines of `logPath` when more diagnostics are required.
